SNAHOME V1.1 - READ.ME file
----------------------------

Welcome to my Home Inventory program V1.1.  This file is for new users only, Users of V1.0 should read README.V10.

The archive should contain the following files:

\APP\SNAHOME1.APP                Main program

\APP\SNAHOME\SNAHOMEH.OVL        Optional Help file
\APP\SNAHOME\SNAHOMEP.OVL        Optional Print file

\OPD\SNAPRINT.DYL                Optional Printer library file

README.NEW          'Get you started' instructions for new users

HISTORY.TXT         Details of the various upgrades the program has gone through.

REGISTER.TXT        Details on how to register the program.
LICENCE.TXT         A legal document

SNAHOME1.TXT        Full instructions in ASCII Text format

I would strongly encourage you to read the instructions, but if you still insist on flying blind:

1.   Put SNAHOME1.APP in your \APP\ directory

2.   If you want to use the optional On-Line Help (Highly recommended) put the file SNAHOMEH.OVL into an \APP\SNAHOME\ directory.

3.   If you want to use the optional Print option put the file SNAHOMEP.OVL into the \APP\SNAHOME\ directory and the file SNAPRINT.DYL into an \OPD\ directory.  Note that this file is common to all my programs, so if you have more than one of them you only need one copy of this file.

4.   Install (PSION-I) and go for it !!

If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions.  I have yet to be asked a question that wasn't already fully explained in the instructions !!

All comments, and registrations, still gratefully received.

If you wish to register, up-to-date details are in the file REGISTER.TXT

If you want to monitor progress on upgrades and enhancements, as well as see if any bugs have been reported, visit the home pages on the World-Wide Web. The addresses are :  

	http://ourworld.compuserve.com/homepages/alanrichey
	or
	http://members.aol.com/alanrichey

If you like the look of the program you may also like to check out my other programs:

A total list is:

For the Siena

    SNACOLLx.ZIP    :  A Collection (records, CDs, books etc) Manager.
    SNADRAWx.ZIP    :  A Drawing/Icon Viewer/Editor.
    SNABANKx.ZIP    :  A Personal Accounts package that includes all of the
                       following smaller programs as optional modules.
                       (Available Oct/Nov 96, see my Home page for details)
    SNAHOMEx.ZIP    :  A Home Inventory program based on the Quicken version.
    SNAFUELx.ZIP    :  A Fuel Consumption Monitor.
    SNAINVx.ZIP     :  An Investment Tracking Program.
    SNAEXPx.ZIP     :  An Expense Account Monitor.
    SNAPLANx.ZIP    :  A Financial Planner similar to that in Quicken

All the programs are also available for the S3A & 3C and just use the prefix 'S3A'
rather then 'SNA'.  There is also an additional program which have not yet been
converted to run on the Siena.  This is:

    S3ATASKx.ZIP    :  An Extended ToDo Manager

('x' denotes a version number)

